    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` response flag so it returns `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349 owners** (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing hard rejection at 50 untouched.\n\nChanges, following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only boolean `capacityWarning` property to the owner schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec).\n\n2. **`ClinicService`** \u2014 declared `isCityApproachingCapacity(String city)`, documented as \"40\u201349 owners inclusive, case-insensitive.\"\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added the `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant and implemented the method as `count >= 40 && count < 50`, reusing the existing case-insensitive `countOwnersInCity` helper (the same count the hard capacity rule uses).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct leaves it to the controller (matching `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 set the flag in `toOwnerDtoWithWarning(...)` from the owner's city, so every owner read (GET and create response) evaluates it against the current city total.\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fills a city to 40, creates one more, expects `capacityWarning: true`) passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
